---
import ProjectLayout from '@/layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Bolt from '@/components/Bolt.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="From Crude to Extrude"
  subtitle="Flagship Research · ISEF 2025"
  role="Lead Researcher & Engineer"
  year="2024–2025"
  tags={[
    'Additive Manufacturing',
    'Recycling',
    'Mechanical Engineering',
    'Electrical Engineering',
    'Systems Engineering',
    'Materials Science',
    'ISEF 2025',
  ]}
  overview="A desktop system combining pultrusion and extrusion into a single machine — recycling PET bottle waste and 3D-printing purge material into additive-manufacturing filament within commercial tolerances, at roughly one-tenth the commercial cost. Built in an at-home workshop over 800 hours, without formal training, using basic tools."
  specs={[
    { key: 'Development time',     value: '800+ hrs' },
    { key: 'Months of build',      value: '8' },
    { key: 'Component iterations', value: '50+' },
    { key: 'CAD-designed parts',   value: '30+' },
    { key: 'Integrated sub-systems', value: '7' },
    { key: 'Energy improvement',   value: '43%' },
    { key: 'Particulate reduction', value: '5×' },
    { key: 'Cost vs. commercial',  value: '~90% cheaper' },
  ]}
  nextProject={{ title: 'Tactile Learning Tiles', href: '/research' }}
  description="Full technical detail on 'From Crude to Extrude' — the ISEF 2025 Regeneron Young Scientist Award-winning desktop plastic recycling system by Benjamin Davis."
>

  <!-- ── The Problem ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">The Problem</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">Plastic waste, expensive filament, and a gap in between</h2>

      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <p class="body-text">
            PET (polyethylene terephthalate) plastic — the material in every clear water bottle —
            is one of the most ubiquitous waste streams on the planet. It's also technically
            recyclable. But in practice, the energy cost and equipment required to re-process it
            into something useful makes small-scale recycling impractical for individuals and
            schools.
          </p>
          <p class="body-text">
            On the other side of the lab bench: commercial 3D-printing filament costs $20–30/kg,
            and every time a printer changes colors it purges material — hundreds of grams of
            clean plastic discarded as waste. No affordable consumer path existed to close
            that loop.
          </p>
          <p class="body-text">
            The question I kept returning to: what would it take to build a machine that
            turns those two waste streams into each other's solution?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="problem-stats">
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-val">$20–30</span>
            <span class="stat-key">Per kg — commercial filament cost</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-val">&lt;$3</span>
            <span class="stat-key">Per kg — this machine's production cost</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-val">PET</span>
            <span class="stat-key">Primary input: bottle waste &amp; 3D purge material</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section proj-section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">The System</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">A novel integration of extrusion and pultrusion</h2>

      <div class="system-grid">
        <div class="system-images">
          <div class="img-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/machine-full.jpg"
              alt="Full From Crude to Extrude system on display at ISEF 2025"
              width="800"
              height="600"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <Bolt position="tl" size={14} />
            <Bolt position="tr" size={14} />
            <span class="img-caption">Full system &middot; ISEF 2025 display</span>
          </div>

          <div class="img-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/machine-detail-auger.jpg"
              alt="Internal components of the recycling machine, showing wiring and subsystem integration"
              width="800"
              height="600"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <span class="img-caption">Internal view &middot; wiring &amp; sub-system integration</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="system-content">
          <p class="body-text">
            Standard filament recycling uses re-extrusion: melt plastic, push it through a die,
            cool it, spool it. The problem is that each thermal cycle degrades the material and
            consumes significant energy for repeated heating. I developed a different approach —
            a novel combination of extrusion and pultrusion that processes material in a single
            pass, reducing thermal cycles and the energy overhead that goes with them.
          </p>

          <p class="body-text">
            The result is a machine with seven integrated sub-systems — spanning electrical,
            mechanical, and chemical engineering — designed entirely in Fusion 360, with 30+
            manufactured parts and 50+ iterated components. Every sub-system had to communicate
            with the others precisely; a tolerance failure in one propagated through the whole
            chain.
          </p>

          <div class="subsystem-table" role="table" aria-label="Integrated sub-systems">
            <p class="sub-table-header">7 Integrated Sub-systems</p>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">01</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Material feeding &amp; preparation</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">02</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Thermal control &amp; heating barrel</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">03</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Auger &amp; extrusion mechanism</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">04</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Pultrusion assembly (novel integration)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">05</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Active cooling &amp; filament forming</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">06</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Diameter measurement &amp; feedback control</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">07</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Motorized spooling &amp; tensioning</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Placeholder: system diagram -->
          <figure
            class="diagram-placeholder"
            data-label="[Diagram: system schematic / sub-system flow — provide engineering drawing or block diagram]"
            aria-label="System diagram placeholder"
          >
            <figcaption>System schematic &mdash; diagram to be added</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Results ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">Results</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">Measured against the standard</h2>

      <p class="body-text" style="max-width:640px; margin-bottom:2rem;">
        All figures measured against standard extrusion and re-extrusion baseline processes.
        Filament diameter tested against commercial specification of ±0.05&thinsp;mm.
      </p>

      <div class="results-table" role="table" aria-label="Quantitative results">
        <div class="results-header" role="row" aria-hidden="true">
          <span role="columnheader">Metric</span>
          <span role="columnheader">Result</span>
          <span role="columnheader">vs. Standard Process</span>
        </div>

        <div class="results-row" role="row">
          <span class="results-metric" role="rowheader">Energy Efficiency</span>
          <span class="results-value copper" role="cell">43% better</span>
          <span class="results-note" role="cell">Fewer thermal cycles; single-pass processing</span>
        </div>

        <div class="results-row" role="row">
          <span class="results-metric" role="rowheader">Particulate Matter</span>
          <span class="results-value copper" role="cell">5&times; less</span>
          <span class="results-note" role="cell">Reduced material degradation through lower thermal exposure</span>
        </div>

        <div class="results-row" role="row">
          <span class="results-metric" role="rowheader">Filament Tolerance</span>
          <span class="results-value gold" role="cell">100% within spec</span>
          <span class="results-note" role="cell">Meets commercial ±0.05&thinsp;mm diameter standard</span>
        </div>

        <div class="results-row" role="row">
          <span class="results-metric" role="rowheader">Production Cost</span>
          <span class="results-value gold" role="cell">~90% cheaper</span>
          <span class="results-note" role="cell">vs. commercial filament at ~$20–30/kg</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Placeholder: results chart -->
      <figure
        class="diagram-placeholder"
        style="margin-top:2rem;"
        data-label="[Chart: energy vs. particulate comparison bar chart — provide data for final chart]"
        aria-label="Results chart placeholder"
      >
        <figcaption>Comparison chart &mdash; to be added with final data</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── The Process ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section proj-section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">The Process</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">800 hours in an at-home workshop</h2>

      <div class="process-grid">
        <div class="process-image">
          <div class="img-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/workshop.jpg"
              alt="Benjamin Davis working in his at-home workshop with grinding sparks"
              width="800"
              height="1000"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <span class="img-caption">At-home workshop &middot; Wrentham, MA</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-text">
          <p class="body-text">
            The machine was built with basic tools in a garage workshop in Wrentham, without
            formal training in machining, electronics design, or chemical engineering. Every
            sub-system was learned from scratch — datasheets, research papers, trial runs,
            and a lot of iterations that didn't work.
          </p>
          <p class="body-text">
            The 50+ component revisions aren't a design flaw — they're the record of a real
            engineering process. Each failure pointed to something specific: a tolerance that
            was off, a thermal property I hadn't accounted for, a mechanical interface that
            needed redesign. I documented everything, because if the process isn't documented,
            it didn't happen.
          </p>
          <p class="body-text">
            8 months. Consecutive all-nighters. Missed weekends. The machine took that long
            to get right, and it was worth the time.
          </p>

          <div class="process-stats" role="table" aria-label="Process statistics">
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Timeline</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">8 months, sophomore–junior year</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Total hours</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">800+ logged hours</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Location</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">At-home workshop, Wrentham, MA</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Tools</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Basic hand tools &amp; shop equipment; no CNC mill</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">CAD</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Fusion 360 — 30+ designed &amp; manufactured parts</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-row" role="row">
              <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Training</span>
              <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Self-taught across all engineering domains</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Recognition ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">Recognition</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">ISEF 2025 and beyond</h2>

      <div class="recognition-grid">
        <div class="recognition-featured">
          <div class="img-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/isef-booth.jpg"
              alt="Benjamin Davis at his ISEF 2025 booth in Columbus, Ohio"
              width="800"
              height="1000"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <span class="img-caption">ISEF 2025 &middot; Columbus, OH &middot; May 2025</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="awards-list">
          <div class="award-block award-block--primary">
            <p class="award-name">Regeneron Young Scientist Award</p>
            <p class="award-event">ISEF 2025 &middot; Columbus, OH</p>
            <p class="award-note">
              One of two students worldwide. 2nd highest overall score at the
              world's largest pre-college science fair.
            </p>
            <p class="award-value">$75,000 scholarship</p>
          </div>

          <div class="award-block">
            <p class="award-name">1st Place — Engineering Technology: Statics &amp; Dynamics</p>
            <p class="award-event">ISEF 2025</p>
          </div>

          <div class="award-block">
            <p class="award-name">1st Place</p>
            <p class="award-event">Massachusetts State Science &amp; Engineering Fair</p>
          </div>

          <div class="award-block">
            <p class="award-name">AMD Engineering Excellence Award</p>
            <p class="award-event">Massachusetts State Science Fair &amp; Region III Science Fair</p>
          </div>

          <div class="award-block">
            <p class="award-name">1st Place &amp; Excellence in Visual Presentation</p>
            <p class="award-event">Bishop Feehan High School Science Fair</p>
          </div>

          <div class="award-block">
            <p class="award-name">Masason Foundation</p>
            <p class="award-event">Global fellowship &mdash; sought out by the Secretariat</p>
          </div>

          <div class="award-block">
            <p class="award-name">AJAS Fellow / AAAS Conference</p>
            <p class="award-event">American Junior Academy of Science &middot; 2026</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── What's Next ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section proj-section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">What's Next</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">The research continues</h2>

      <div class="next-table" role="table" aria-label="Future research directions">
        <div class="spec-row" role="row">
          <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Composite filament</span>
          <span class="spec-val" role="cell">
            Coaxial hollow double-material water-cooled auger for composite extrusion (e.g., PEEK+PLA)
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-row" role="row">
          <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Metal extrusion</span>
          <span class="spec-val" role="cell">
            Aluminum bar extrusion at maker scale — bringing metal forming out of the factory
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-row" role="row">
          <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Benchmarking</span>
          <span class="spec-val" role="cell">
            Rigorous comparison against commercial filament production solutions
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-row" role="row">
          <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">IP</span>
          <span class="spec-val" role="cell">
            Patenting the extrusion-pultrusion combination method
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-row" role="row">
          <span class="spec-key" role="rowheader">Deployment</span>
          <span class="spec-val" role="cell">
            Commercialization and implementation in schools and makerspaces
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Photo gallery ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="proj-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">Gallery</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">From the build and competition</h2>

      <div class="gallery-grid">
        <div class="gallery-item">
          <img
            src="/images/isef-award.jpg"
            alt="Benjamin Davis at his science fair display board with the machine"
            width="800"
            height="600"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <p class="gallery-caption">Science fair display &middot; State competition</p>
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-item">
          <img
            src="/images/machine-detail-auger.jpg"
            alt="Detailed view of the machine internals showing wiring and subsystem components"
            width="800"
            height="600"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <p class="gallery-caption">Internal wiring &amp; sub-system integration</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Placeholder: filament output close-up -->
        <figure
          class="gallery-item gallery-placeholder"
          data-label="[Photo: machine-detail-filament.jpg — close-up of filament output/spool · 1200×800]"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Filament output photo — not yet provided"
        >
          <figcaption>Filament output &mdash; photo coming soon</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</ProjectLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Section wrappers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .proj-section {
    padding-block: 4.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }

  .proj-section--dark {
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .overline {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--copper);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .section-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .body-text {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.78;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .body-text:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ── Shared spec rows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .spec-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }
  .spec-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .spec-key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--copper);
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--graphite) 40%, var(--panel));
  }

  .spec-val {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
  }

  /* ── Image frame ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .img-frame {
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .img-frame img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: brightness(0.88) contrast(1.07);
  }

  .img-caption {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--steel);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--graphite) 90%, transparent);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }

  /* ── Diagram / chart placeholders ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  .diagram-placeholder {
    border: 1px dashed var(--panel-edge);
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .diagram-placeholder::before {
    content: attr(data-label);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--steel);
    opacity: 0.55;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .diagram-placeholder figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    color: var(--panel-edge);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── The Problem ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 220px;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .problem-stats {
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .stat-item {
    padding: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }
  .stat-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .stat-val {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--gold);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stat-key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--steel);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* ── The System ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .system-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .system-images {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .subsystem-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
  }

  .sub-table-header {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--copper);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--graphite) 80%, var(--panel));
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .system-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* ── Results table ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .results-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }

  .results-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px 140px 1fr;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--panel-edge);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--graphite) 70%, var(--panel));
  }

  .results-header span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--copper);
    padding: 0 0.85rem;
  }

  .results-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px 140px 1fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
  }
  .results-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .results-metric {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--steel);
    padding: 0.85rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .results-value {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1;
    padding: 0.75rem 0.85rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--panel-edge);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .results-value.copper { color: var(--copper); }
  .results-value.gold   { color: var(--gold);   }

  .results-note {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
